{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 16, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the sunlight oddly pixelated as it streamed through his window. He sat up in bed, a strange awareness flooding him – the texture of the sheets felt…scripted. He glanced at his hands, noticing a slight shimmer, like a low-resolution rendering issue. A notification box, impossibly, popped into his vision: \"Welcome to Aethelgard! Level 1: The Shirewood.\" Panic seized him. The quaint cottage he’d always dreamed of owning was now…perfectly, unnervingly perfect. He tried to reach for his glasses, but his arm moved with a strange, predictable fluidity, as if guided by unseen code. A deer grazed peacefully in the garden, its movements too smooth, too repetitive. This wasn't real. This *couldn't* be real.\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled outside, the world resolving into sharp, almost cartoonish detail. A cheerful villager, with an unnervingly wide smile, greeted him with the phrase \"Greetings, Adventurer! Are you ready to begin your quest?\" Quest? Adventurer? Arthur wanted to scream. He instinctively checked his inventory – a leather tunic, a rusty sword, and a suspiciously large healing potion. He was trapped, a character in someone else’s meticulously crafted world. The cheerful villager gestured towards a path leading into the Shirewood, a quest marker hovering above his head. Arthur sighed, a wave of despair washing over him. He had a feeling this was going to be a very long game.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.16696929931640625}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.407365083694458}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.00015984688070602715}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.08786557614803314}, {"token": "▁sunlight", "logprob": -1.4177302122116089}, {"token": "▁oddly", "logprob": -2.4148879051208496}, {"token": "▁pixel", "logprob": -1.2452977895736694}, {"token": "ated", "logprob": -4.410646579344757e-05}, {"token": "▁as", "logprob":